// Strategy modules — spec build-order item 22, PHASE 23.
//
// A reusable economic module declares all eight things the phase requires:
// inputs, outputs, effects, guarantees, permissions, required domains, a risk
// profile and resource bounds. Eight required lines would be decoration if
// nothing read them, so each one is checked against the body:
//
// - `effects [swap]` must be discharged by `execute` — a module that claims to
//   swap and does not is claiming work it does not do.
// - `guarantees [min_profit]` needs a *floor* in the body (`require profit >= 5`).
//   Written as a ceiling it would say the opposite, and the check reads the
//   operator, not just the number.
// - `domains [ethereum]` must cover every chain the body touches.
// - the risk profile must bound what the body accepts: a body relying on
//   `require slippage <= 900` while the module declares `max_slippage_bps 50`
//   contradicts its own declaration.
// - `permissions` are a ceiling on the body, not a wish list: touching more than
//   one chain needs `cross_domain`, and opting into netting needs
//   `intent_fusion`.
//
// Note what is *absent*: `permissions`, because this module uses none. An empty
// clause is refused by the parser — omitting it says the same thing more
// clearly — and the compiler still checks that the body does nothing it did not
// declare.

strategy TriDexArb {
    input ethereum.USDC amount 25_000_000
    output ethereum.ETH
    effects [swap]
    guarantees [min_profit]
    domains [ethereum]
    risk { max_slippage_bps 50 max_total_fee_bps 8 }
    bounds { max_steps 10 max_gas 200_000 }
    execute {
        swap uniswap ethereum.USDC -> ethereum.ETH amount 1_000 min_output 1
        require slippage <= 50
        require profit >= 5
        on_fail refund ethereum.USDC to sender
    }
}
